# My CV

A personal CV presented as an Android app. Browse an introduction, skills, career experience, education, and contact details in a mobile-first interface built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.

> Project: Android portfolio / CV app  
> Platform: Android 7.0 (API 24) and later

## Explore

The app organizes CV information into these sections:

- Introduction — a personal profile and overview
- Skills — skills with proficiency indicators
- Career — professional experience
- Education — education history
- Contact — contact information

## Built with

- Kotlin
- Jetpack Compose and Material 3
- Navigation Compose
- AndroidX
- Gradle

## Run the app

### Requirements

- Android Studio with Android SDK 33 installed
- An Android emulator or physical device running API 24 or later

### In Android Studio

1. Clone this repository and open it in Android Studio.
2. Allow the Gradle project to sync.
3. Select an emulator or connected Android device.
4. Run the `app` configuration.

### From the command line

Build a debug APK:

```bash
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

On Windows:

```bat
gradlew.bat assembleDebug
```

Run the local unit tests:

```bash
./gradlew test
```

Run instrumentation tests on a connected device or emulator:

```bash
./gradlew connectedAndroidTest
```

## Project layout

```text
app/src/main/java/com/example/mycv/
├── data/       # CV data models
└── ui/
    ├── home/   # Introduction, skills, career, education, and contact screens
    ├── navigation/
    └── theme/
```

Android resources are in `app/src/main/res/`. The Android app module and SDK settings are configured in `app/build.gradle`.

## Configuration

The app currently targets Android API 33, supports API 24 and later, and uses `com.example.mycv` as its application ID. Adjust these values in `app/build.gradle` if you are adapting the project for your own CV.

